# STEP 11: Configure Nagios to Monitor the Web Application (Additional)

For a complete monitoring demonstration, Nagios must have a check for Nginx.

The web application is reachable internally at:

```text
http://web:80
```

Nagios can use a plugin such as `check_http` to check whether the web server responds successfully.

A Nagios service configuration can look like this:

```text
define host {
    use             linux-server
    host_name       web
    alias           OLMS Web Application
    address         web
}

define service {
    use                     generic-service
    host_name               web
    service_description     HTTP Monitoring
    check_command           check_http!-p 80
}
```

Save this in the appropriate Nagios configuration directory and ensure the configuration is included in `nagios.cfg`.

The image stores its Nagios configuration under:

```text
/opt/nagios/etc
```

After updating the configuration, validate and reload Nagios.

**Note:** This is an additional configuration step. The two-container deployment works without it, but the actual HTTP monitoring check will not appear automatically.

