  - "5000:5000"
```

| Port | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 5000 (left) | Host port |
| 5000 (right) | Container port |

### 4. Nginx service

```yaml
nginx:
  image: nginx:alpine
```

Uses the lightweight Nginx Docker image.

### 5. Nginx port mapping

```yaml
ports:
  - "80:80"
```

| Port | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 80 (left) | Host port |
| 80 (right) | Container port |

### 6. Volumes

```yaml
volumes:
  - ./nginx/nginx.conf:/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf:ro
```

Mounts our Nginx configuration file inside the container.

`ro` means read-only.

### 7. depends_on

```yaml
depends_on:
  - flask
```

Starts Flask before Nginx.

Remember: Basic `depends_on` controls startup order but does not guarantee Flask is ready to accept requests.

### 8. Network

```yaml
networks:
  - food-network
```

Connects both containers to the same Docker network.

### 9. Restart

```yaml
restart: always
```

Automatically restarts the container when it stops.

